/**
\page org_mitk_views_dicomtractogramtageditor DICOM Tractogram Tag Editor

Tractograms saved as DICOM tractography results (supplement 181 of the DICOM standard, .dcm) refer to the image they were computed from and carry the patient and study of that image. This view shows and edits these DICOM tags of the tractogram selected in its combo box: patient ID and name, study, series and SOP instance UID, SOP class UID and frame of reference UID of the referenced image, and the codes of the tracking algorithm family, the model and the anatomy.

A value is edited by double-clicking it in the table. "Copy Properties From Image" copies the reference tags (patient, study, series, SOP instance and class, frame of reference) from the image selected in the Data Manager, e.g. the diffusion-weighted image the tractogram was computed from. Tags the image does not have keep their value and are listed in a message.

When the tractogram is saved as DICOM, the writer uses these tags; the tractogram itself gets new series and SOP instance UIDs. Tags that are still missing are written as "0", and missing study and frame of reference UIDs are generated with a warning.

*/
